#: landing/templates/landing/acceptable_use.html:19
msgid "VPNsterr (operated by <strong>Sterr Technologies</strong>) exists to protect privacy. That mission only works if the network isn't abused. By using the free extension or a Premium subscription you agree to this policy, which forms part of our <a href=\"/terms/\" class=\"underline\">Terms of Service</a>."
msgstr ""

#: landing/templates/landing/acceptable_use.html:22
msgid "1) You may"
msgstr ""

#: landing/templates/landing/acceptable_use.html:24
msgid "Use the service for personal privacy, security on public networks, and accessing content available to you."
msgstr ""

#: landing/templates/landing/acceptable_use.html:25
msgid "Use it on the number of devices your plan allows, for yourself and your household."
msgstr ""

#: landing/templates/landing/acceptable_use.html:30
msgid "2) You may not use the service to"
msgstr ""

#: landing/templates/landing/acceptable_use.html:32
msgid "Break the law of the jurisdiction you are in, or facilitate others doing so."
msgstr ""

#: landing/templates/landing/acceptable_use.html:33
msgid "Send spam, run phishing campaigns, distribute malware, or operate botnets / command-and-control infrastructure."
msgstr ""

#: landing/templates/landing/acceptable_use.html:34
msgid "Attack networks or systems: DDoS, unauthorized access attempts, port scanning of third parties, exploitation of vulnerabilities you are not authorized to test."
msgstr ""

#: landing/templates/landing/acceptable_use.html:35
msgid "Access, share or distribute child sexual abuse material — zero tolerance; accounts are terminated and reported where the law requires."
msgstr ""

#: landing/templates/landing/acceptable_use.html:36
msgid "Infringe intellectual property rights at scale, engage in fraud, harassment, or identity theft."
msgstr ""

#: landing/templates/landing/acceptable_use.html:37
msgid "Resell, rent or commercially redistribute the service without a written agreement with Sterr Technologies."
msgstr ""

#: landing/templates/landing/acceptable_use.html:38
msgid "Interfere with the network itself: probing our infrastructure, evading device limits, or degrading service for other users."
msgstr ""

#: landing/templates/landing/acceptable_use.html:43
msgid "3) Enforcement — how it works with zero logs"
msgstr ""

#: landing/templates/landing/acceptable_use.html:44
msgid "We do not log your browsing activity, so enforcement is based on real-time signals (such as abuse reports tied to shared exit IPs and automated volumetric anomalies), never on stored activity history. We may suspend or terminate accounts involved in abuse, throttle abusive flows in real time, and block destinations subject to repeated abuse complaints."
msgstr ""

#: landing/templates/landing/acceptable_use.html:48
msgid "4) Reporting abuse"
msgstr ""

#: landing/templates/landing/acceptable_use.html:49
msgid "To report abuse originating from our network, contact <a href=\"mailto:support@vpnsterr.com\" class=\"underline\">support@vpnsterr.com</a> with timestamps, IPs and evidence. We respond to all legitimate reports."
msgstr ""

#: landing/templates/landing/acceptable_use.html:53
msgid "5) Changes"
msgstr ""

#: landing/templates/landing/acceptable_use.html:54
msgid "We may update this policy; material changes are posted on this page with a new \\"
msgstr ""

